{"id":"mahabharata-2-046","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":46,"title":"षट्चत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 46 · Duryodhana describes his envy","summary":{"en":"Janamejaya asks how the fateful game came about. Vaishampayana relates how Duryodhana, alone with his father, says that a man who does not resent his rival's prosperity is the lowest of men, and describes the treasures he saw at the sacrifice.","kn":"ಆ ವಿನಾಶಕಾರಿ ಜೂಜು ಹೇಗೆ ನಡೆಯಿತೆಂದು ಜನಮೇಜಯನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತಂದೆಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ಏಕಾಂತದಲ್ಲಿ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನು, ಶತ್ರುವಿನ ಏಳಿಗೆಯನ್ನು ಸಹಿಸುವವನು ಅಧಮ ಎಂದು ಹೇಳಿ, ಯಜ್ಞದಲ್ಲಿ ಕಂಡ ಸಂಪತ್ತನ್ನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುವುದನ್ನು ವೈಶಂಪಾಯನನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"जनमेजय पूछते हैं कि वह विनाशकारी द्यूत कैसे हुआ। वैशम्पायन बताते हैं कि पिता के साथ एकान्त में दुर्योधन कहता है कि जो शत्रु की समृद्धि पर क्रोध न करे वह अधम पुरुष है, और यज्ञ में देखे खज़ानों का वर्णन करता है।","te":"ఆ వినాశకర జూదం ఎలా జరిగిందని జనమేజయుడు అడుగుతాడు. తండ్రితో ఏకాంతంలో దుర్యోధనుడు, శత్రువు అభివృద్ధిపై కోపించనివాడు అధముడని చెప్పి, యజ్ఞంలో చూసిన సంపదలను వర్ణించడాన్ని వైశంపాయనుడు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"அந்த அழிவுச் சூது எப்படி நடந்தது என்று ஜனமேஜயன் கேட்கிறான். தந்தையுடன் தனிமையில் துரியோதனன், பகைவனின் வளத்தைக் கண்டு சினக்காதவன் இழிந்தவன் என்று சொல்லி, யாகத்தில் கண்ட செல்வங்களை வர்ணிப்பதை வைஶம்பாயனர் சொல்கிறார்.","ml":"ദുര്യോധനന്റെ പ്രസിദ്ധമായ ചൂതുകളിയുടെ ഉത്ഭവം ജനമേജയൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. പിതാവുമായി തനിച്ചിരിക്കുമ്പോൾ, സഹോദരന്റെ ഐശ്വര്യത്തിൽ അസൂയപ്പെടാത്തവൻ മനുഷ്യരിൽ അധമനാണെന്ന് ദുര്യോധനൻ പറയുന്നതും, യജ്ഞത്തിൽ താൻ കണ്ട നിധികളെക്കുറിച്ച് വിവരിക്കുന്നതും വൈശമ്പായനൻ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.46; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"द्यूतपर्व","titleEn":"Dyuta Parva (The dice game)","verses":[{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कथं समभवद्द्यूतं भ्रातॄणां तन्महात्ययम् ।\nयत्र तद्व्यसनं प्राप्तं पाण्डवैर्मे पितामहैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How did that gambling among brothers come about, so ruinous, in which my grandfathers the Pandavas met with disaster?"}},{"n":2,"text":"के च तत्र सभास्तारा राजानो ब्रह्मवित्तम ।\nके चैनमन्वमोदन्त के चैनं प्रत्यषेधयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of knowers of Brahman, who were the kings in that hall, who approved of the game, and who opposed it?"}},{"n":3,"text":"विस्तरेणैतदिच्छामि कथ्यमानं त्वया द्विज ।\nमूलं ह्येतद्विनाशस्य पृथिव्या द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmin, I wish you to tell this in detail, for it was the root of the destruction of the earth, best of the twice-born."}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तदा राज्ञा व्यासशिष्यः प्रतापवान् ।\nआचचक्षे यथावृत्तं तत्सर्वं सर्ववेदवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by the king, the mighty disciple of Vyasa, who knew all the Vedas, told it all as it happened."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"शृणु मे विस्तरेणेमां कथां भरतसत्तम ।\nभूय एव महाराज यदि ते श्रवणे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear from me in detail this story, best of the Bharatas, great king, if your mind is set on hearing it."}},{"n":6,"text":"विदुरस्य मतं ज्ञात्वा धृतराष्ट्रोऽम्बिकासुतः ।\nदुर्योधनमिदं वाक्यमुवाच विजने पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing Vidura's opinion, Dhritarashtra, son of Ambika, again spoke to Duryodhana in private:"}},{"n":7,"text":"अलं द्यूतेन गान्धारे विदुरो न प्रशंसति ।\nन ह्यसौ सुमहाबुद्धिरहितं नो वदिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said: Enough of gambling, son of Gandhari; Vidura does not praise it. That very wise man would not tell us what harms us."}},{"n":8,"text":"हितं हि परमं मन्ये विदुरो यत्प्रभाषते ।\nक्रियतां पुत्र तत्सर्वमेतन्मन्ये हितं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think what Vidura says is the highest good. Son, do all that; I think it is for your benefit."}},{"n":9,"text":"देवर्षिर्वासवगुरुर्देवराजाय धीमते ।\nयत्प्राह शास्त्रं भगवान्बृहस्पतिरुदारधीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What the blessed Brihaspati, divine sage and teacher of Indra, of noble mind, taught the wise king of the gods in his treatise,"}},{"n":10,"text":"तद्वेद विदुरः सर्वं सरहस्यं महाकविः ।\nस्थितश्च वचने तस्य सदाहमपि पुत्रक ॥","meaning":{"en":"all of it Vidura, the great poet, knows, with its secrets, and I too, son, always abide by his word."}},{"n":11,"text":"विदुरो वापि मेधावी कुरूणां प्रवरो मतः ।\nउद्धवो वा महाबुद्धिर्वृष्णीनामर्चितो नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vidura is thought the wisest and best of the Kurus, as Uddhava of great intelligence is honoured among the Vrishnis, king."}},{"n":12,"text":"द्यूतेन तदलं पुत्र द्यूते भेदो हि दृश्यते ।\nभेदे विनाशो राज्यस्य तत्पुत्र परिवर्जय ॥","meaning":{"en":"So enough of dice, son; in gambling a rift is seen, and from a rift comes ruin of the kingdom; so avoid it."}},{"n":13,"text":"पित्रा मात्रा च पुत्रस्य यद्वै कार्यं परं स्मृतम् ।\nप्राप्तस्त्वमसि तत्तात पितृपैतामहं पदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What a father and mother consider the highest duty toward a son, son, you have reached: your father's and grandfather's place."}},{"n":14,"text":"अधीतवान्कृती शास्त्रे लालितः सततं गृहे ।\nभ्रातृज्येष्ठः स्थितो राज्ये विन्दसे किं न शोभनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Learned, accomplished in scripture, always cherished at home, eldest of your brothers, and established in the kingdom, what good thing do you not have?"}},{"n":15,"text":"पृथग्जनैरलभ्यं यद्भोजनाच्छादनं परम् ।\nतत्प्राप्तोऽसि महाबाहो कस्माच्छोचसि पुत्रक ॥","meaning":{"en":"The finest food and clothing, unattainable by ordinary people, you have obtained, mighty-armed; why do you grieve, son?"}},{"n":16,"text":"स्फीतं राष्ट्रं महाबाहो पितृपैतामहं महत् ।\nनित्यमाज्ञापयन्भासि दिवि देवेश्वरो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great and prosperous kingdom of your father and grandfather is yours, mighty-armed; always commanding, you shine like the lord of gods in heaven."}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्य ते विदितप्रज्ञ शोकमूलमिदं कथम् ।\nसमुत्थितं दुःखतरं तन्मे शंसितुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wise one, how has this root of sorrow arisen, a worse affliction? You should tell me."}},{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"अश्नाम्याच्छादयामीति प्रपश्यन्पापपूरुषः ।\nनामर्षं कुरुते यस्तु पुरुषः सोऽधमः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said: The wretched man who says, I eat and I dress, and looking on feels no anger, is said to be the lowest of men."}},{"n":19,"text":"न मां प्रीणाति राजेन्द्र लक्ष्मीः साधारणा विभो ।\nज्वलितामिव कौन्तेये श्रियं दृष्ट्वा च विव्यथे ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, a prosperity shared with others does not please me, lord; seeing the Pandava's fortune blazing, I am tormented."}},{"n":20,"text":"सर्वां हि पृथिवीं दृष्ट्वा युधिष्ठिरवशानुगाम् ।\nस्थिरोऽस्मि योऽहं जीवामि दुःखादेतद्ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the whole earth following Yudhishthira's will, I stand firm, I who still live; I tell you this out of pain."}},{"n":21,"text":"आवर्जिता इवाभान्ति निघ्नाश्चैत्रकिकौकुराः ।\nकारस्करा लोहजङ्घा युधिष्ठिरनिवेशने ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Nipas, Chaitrakas, Kaukuras, Karaskaras and Lohajanghas seem to bow down in Yudhishthira's house."}},{"n":22,"text":"हिमवत्सागरानूपाः सर्वरत्नाकरास्तथा ।\nअन्त्याः सर्वे पर्युदस्ता युधिष्ठिरनिवेशने ॥","meaning":{"en":"The people of the Himalaya and the sea marshes, and those from all mines of jewels, even the lowest, were all sent to Yudhishthira's house."}},{"n":23,"text":"ज्येष्ठोऽयमिति मां मत्वा श्रेष्ठश्चेति विशां पते ।\nयुधिष्ठिरेण सत्कृत्य युक्तो रत्नपरिग्रहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Considering me the eldest and the best, king, Yudhishthira honoured me and put me in charge of receiving the jewels."}},{"n":24,"text":"उपस्थितानां रत्नानां श्रेष्ठानामर्घहारिणाम् ।\nनादृश्यत परः प्रान्तो नापरस्तत्र भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of the best and most priceless jewels that were brought, no end or limit was seen there, Bharata."}},{"n":25,"text":"न मे हस्तः समभवद्वसु तत्प्रतिगृह्णतः ।\nप्रातिष्ठन्त मयि श्रान्ते गृह्य दूराहृतं वसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"My hand could not keep up with receiving that wealth; I grew tired, and they went away carrying it, brought from afar."}},{"n":26,"text":"कृतां बिन्दुसरोरत्नैर्मयेन स्फाटिकच्छदाम् ।\nअपश्यं नलिनीं पूर्णामुदकस्येव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Made by Maya of jewels from Bindu lake, with a crystal covering, I saw a lotus pond that looked full of water, Bharata."}},{"n":27,"text":"वस्त्रमुत्कर्षति मयि प्राहसत्स वृकोदरः ।\nशत्रोरृद्धिविशेषेण विमूढं रत्नवर्जितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I lifted my clothes, Vrikodara laughed, at me, bewildered and bereft of jewels, by the special prosperity of my enemy."}},{"n":28,"text":"तत्र स्म यदि शक्तः स्यां पातयेयं वृकोदरम् ।\nसपत्नेनावहासो हि स मां दहति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I had been able, I would have struck Vrikodara down there; for mockery by a rival burns me, Bharata."}},{"n":29,"text":"पुनश्च तादृशीमेव वापीं जलजशालिनीम् ।\nमत्वा शिलासमां तोये पतितोऽस्मि नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"And again, taking another such pond, full of lotuses, for a stone floor, I fell in the water, lord of men."}},{"n":30,"text":"तत्र मां प्राहसत्कृष्णः पार्थेन सह सस्वनम् ।\nद्रौपदी च सह स्त्रीभिर्व्यथयन्ती मनो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Krishna laughed loudly with Partha, and Draupadi with her women, wounding my heart."}},{"n":31,"text":"क्लिन्नवस्त्रस्य च जले किंकरा राजचोदिताः ।\nददुर्वासांसि मेऽन्यानि तच्च दुःखतरं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"When my clothes were wet, servants, directed by the king, gave me other clothes, and that was even more painful."}},{"n":32,"text":"प्रलम्भं च शृणुष्वान्यं गदतो मे नराधिप ।\nअद्वारेण विनिर्गच्छन्द्वारसंस्थानरूपिणा ।\nअभिहत्य शिलां भूयो ललाटेनास्मि विक्षतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear another deception, as I tell it, lord of men: going out through a door that was only a painted door shape, I struck the stone again and hurt my forehead."}},{"n":33,"text":"तत्र मां यमजौ दूरादालोक्य ललितौ किल ।\nबाहुभिः परिगृह्णीतां शोचन्तौ सहितावुभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the twins Nakula and Sahadeva, seeing me from afar, charmingly caught me in their arms, both together, grieving."}},{"n":34,"text":"उवाच सहदेवस्तु तत्र मां विस्मयन्निव ।\nइदं द्वारमितो गच्छ राजन्निति पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sahadeva, as though wondering, said to me there again and again: King, go this way, here is the door."}},{"n":35,"text":"नामधेयानि रत्नानां पुरस्तान्न श्रुतानि मे ।\nयानि दृष्टानि मे तस्यां मनस्तपति तच्च मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I had never before heard the names of the jewels; what I saw in that hall torments my mind."}}]}]}